From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:19:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: publish the SMC's
 voltage and current channels

The J604's SMC also updates 55 readable voltage and current keys that
Linux never reads, next to the power keys published in
t8132-j604-hwmon-rails.dtsi.

Add them from the same macOS 26B123 key sweep (readable 4-byte floats
whose value moved between two reads 20 s apart on an idle desktop): 23
voltage and 32 current keys, labelled by family as the power keys are,
since their consumers are not mapped on this machine. A key the running
SMC firmware does not offer is skipped by the driver.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
